    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field derived from the locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table, returned as an IANA name.\n\nThe codebase already derives an owner's region (as `locality`) and exposes derived fields through generated DTOs, so the change followed that existing pattern with two edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a fixed `REGION_TIMEZONE` map (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) and a `@Transient getTimezone()` that looks up the owner's `getLocality()`/region in it (returning `null` when the region has no mapped timezone).\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `timezone` read-only string property to the `Owner` response schema, right after `locality`.\n\nNo mapper or OfficeFloor YAML changes were needed: MapStruct auto-maps `getTimezone()` to the generated DTO's `timezone` field by name, and the existing `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}` pipeline (`LoadOwner \u2192 \u2026 \u2192 RespondWithOwner`) carries it automatically \u2014 the same way `locality` works.\n\n**Verification:** the full test suite passes \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`. The pinned acceptance test `coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` now sees `$.locality == \"NSW\"` and `$.timezone == \"Australia/Sydney\"` for a Sydney owner with postcode 2000.",
