    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits the existing structure cleanly:\n\n- `REGION_TIMEZONE` sits alongside the other fixed lookup tables (`CITY_REGION`, `REGION_RANGE`) and follows the same `Map.of(...)` shape and Javadoc style.\n- `getTimezone()` mirrors the other `@Transient` derived getters (`getLocality()`, `getMembershipLevel()`) in placement, documentation, and \"not persisted \u2014 derived from X\" convention.\n- It reuses `getLocality()` as the region source rather than re-deriving the region, so there's no duplication of the region-resolution logic, and returning `null` for an unmapped region matches the spec's \"absent when the region has no mapped timezone\" (consistent with the `readOnly`/absent handling in the OpenAI schema entry).\n- The OpenAPI addition is placed next to the related `locality` field and is consistent with the surrounding entries.\n\nA maintainer of this file would find this a natural extension of the established derived-attribute pattern.",
